---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-decor" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="blob blob-blue"></span>
        <span class="blob blob-coral"></span>
        <span class="blob blob-yellow"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="container hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">
            <span>AI delivery</span>
            <span>Odoo</span>
            <span>OWL</span>
            <span>OCA</span>
          </p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Odoo, AI, and OWL tools that <mark>remove the busywork</mark>.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lede">Python and Odoo fullstack developer. I build AI-assisted delivery tools, ship Odoo modules and migrations, experiment with OWL, and review work in the Odoo Community Association.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="#proof">See the proof</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="#oca">Explore the OCA wins</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-meta">Based in Cuba <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Working worldwide <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> English / Español</p>
          <ul class="hero-chips" aria-label="Core stack">
            <li>AI agents</li>
            <li>Odoo 8→19</li>
            <li>OWL</li>
            <li>OCA</li>
            <li>Python</li>
            <li>TypeScript</li>
            <li>Go</li>
            <li>Lua</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <aside class="scoreboard" aria-label="Verified public results">
          <div class="scoreboard-head">
            <span>Public proof</span>
            <span>2022—2026</span>
          </div>
          <dl class="score-grid">
            <div class="score score-blue">
              <dt>Merged PRs</dt>
              <dd>290</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="score score-coral">
              <dt>OCA merges</dt>
              <dd>10</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="score score-green">
              <dt>Reviews</dt>
              <dd>78</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="score score-yellow">
              <dt>ODF tests</dt>
              <dd>1,477</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <figure class="merge-card">
            <svg class="merge-wall" viewBox="0 0 290 100" role="img" aria-labelledby="wall-title wall-desc">
              <title id="wall-title">290 merged pull requests</title>
              <desc id="wall-desc">A wall of 290 tiles, one for every merged pull request. Ten tiles are highlighted in coral to represent the ten merged contributions to the Odoo Community Association.</desc>
              <defs>
                <pattern id="merge-tile" width="10" height="10" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
                  <rect x="1" y="1" width="8" height="8" rx="1" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.3"></rect>
                </pattern>
              </defs>
              <rect width="290" height="100" fill="url(#merge-tile)"></rect>
              <g class="oca-tiles" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect x="21" y="11" width="8" height="8" rx="1"></rect>
                <rect x="51" y="21" width="8" height="8" rx="1"></rect>
                <rect x="81" y="11" width="8" height="8" rx="1"></rect>
                <rect x="111" y="31" width="8" height="8" rx="1"></rect>
                <rect x="141" y="21" width="8" height="8" rx="1"></rect>
                <rect x="171" y="41" width="8" height="8" rx="1"></rect>
                <rect x="201" y="11" width="8" height="8" rx="1"></rect>
                <rect x="231" y="31" width="8" height="8" rx="1"></rect>
                <rect x="261" y="21" width="8" height="8" rx="1"></rect>
                <rect x="281" y="41" width="8" height="8" rx="1"></rect>
              </g>
            </svg>
            <figcaption>290 merged pull requests. Every tile is one. Ten are in OCA.</figcaption>
            <p class="merge-meta">365 authored <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> 79% merge rate</p>
          </figure>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <div class="win-ticker" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ticker-track">
          <span>290 merged PRs</span><span>10 OCA merges</span><span>53 OCA reviews</span><span>1,477 unit tests</span><span>520× faster</span><span>8→19 Odoo</span><span>10 releases</span><span>9★ OWL</span>
          <span>290 merged PRs</span><span>10 OCA merges</span><span>53 OCA reviews</span><span>1,477 unit tests</span><span>520× faster</span><span>8→19 Odoo</span><span>10 releases</span><span>9★ OWL</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section focus-section" id="focus" aria-labelledby="focus-title">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="section-label">01 / Focus</p>
          <h2 id="focus-title">Four things I keep making better.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">AI delivery, Odoo engineering, OWL frontends, and OCA collaboration. Each one has public receipts, not a slide deck.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="focus-grid">
          <article class="focus-card focus-ai">
            <span class="focus-number">01</span>
            <p class="focus-kicker">AI delivery</p>
            <h3>ODF Agent Team</h3>
            <p>Spec-driven Odoo delivery on OpenCode. Eleven specialist agents, fifty-one skills, and policy gates that make AI work reviewable instead of magical.</p>
            <ul class="focus-stats">
              <li><strong>11</strong> agents</li>
              <li><strong>51</strong> skills</li>
              <li><strong>1,477</strong> tests</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="focus-link" href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/odf-agent-team">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>

          <article class="focus-card focus-odoo">
            <span class="focus-number">02</span>
            <p class="focus-kicker">Odoo engineering</p>
            <h3>Modules and migrations, 8 to 19.</h3>
            <p>EasyPost, Plaid, POS, reporting, website, and localization changes. The kind of work that has to survive an OCA review and a real upgrade.</p>
            <ul class="focus-stats">
              <li><strong>8→19</strong> Odoo</li>
              <li><strong>10</strong> merged</li>
              <li><strong>37</strong> submitted</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="focus-link" href="#oca">Read the OCA ledger <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>

          <article class="focus-card focus-owl">
            <span class="focus-number">03</span>
            <p class="focus-kicker">OWL frontend</p>
            <h3>Hacking OWL</h3>
            <p>A custom OWL web client and reusable components, built to understand the framework from the inside instead of treating it as a black box.</p>
            <ul class="focus-stats">
              <li><strong>9★</strong> GitHub</li>
              <li><strong>Apache-2.0</strong></li>
              <li><strong>OWL</strong></li>
            </ul>
            <a class="focus-link" href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/hacking-owl">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>

          <article class="focus-card focus-oca">
            <span class="focus-number">04</span>
            <p class="focus-kicker">OCA collaboration</p>
            <h3>Ten merged changes. Eight repositories.</h3>
            <p>37 pull requests submitted, 10 merged, and 53 reviews across 26 repositories and 22 authors. Teamwork, in public.</p>
            <ul class="focus-stats">
              <li><strong>10</strong> merged</li>
              <li><strong>8</strong> repos</li>
              <li><strong>53</strong> reviews</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="focus-link" href="#oca">See every merged change <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section wins-section" id="proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="section-label">02 / Proof</p>
          <h2 id="proof-title">The wins, without the scavenger hunt.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">Eight public numbers that explain the work before the first scroll. No private repositories, no inflated line counts, no borrowed stars.</p>
        </header>

        <ul class="wins-grid" aria-label="Verified wins">
          <li class="win win-blue"><strong>290</strong><span>merged pull requests</span></li>
          <li class="win win-coral"><strong>79%</strong><span>merge rate</span></li>
          <li class="win win-green"><strong>10</strong><span>OCA merges</span></li>
          <li class="win win-yellow"><strong>53</strong><span>OCA reviews</span></li>
          <li class="win win-plum"><strong>1,477</strong><span>ODF unit tests</span></li>
          <li class="win win-blue"><strong>520×</strong><span>faster OSEM</span></li>
          <li class="win win-coral"><strong>8→19</strong><span>Odoo versions</span></li>
          <li class="win win-green"><strong>9★</strong><span>Hacking OWL</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section work-section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="section-label">03 / Selected work</p>
          <h2 id="work-title">Tools that remove the guesswork.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">Six public projects across five languages. Each one started with a repeated annoyance and ended with something other people can use.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="project-grid">
          <article class="project project-featured project-ai">
            <div class="project-topline">
              <p class="project-kind">Flagship <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> AI + TypeScript</p>
              <p class="project-badge">1,477 tests</p>
            </div>
            <h3>ODF Agent Team</h3>
            <p class="project-copy">Spec-driven Odoo delivery on OpenCode. Eleven specialist agents, fifty-one skills, policy gates, and 1,477 unit tests, so the work is found instead of invented.</p>
            <div class="pipeline" aria-label="ODF stage pipeline">
              <span>Decide</span><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><span>Plan</span><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><span>Build</span><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><span>Verify</span>
            </div>
            <dl class="project-stats">
              <div><dt>Unit tests</dt><dd>1,477</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Releases</dt><dd>10</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Stars / forks</dt><dd>14 / 7</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="project-link" href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/odf-agent-team">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>

          <article class="project project-odoo">
            <p class="project-kind">Odoo <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Lua + Neovim</p>
            <h3>odoo.nvim</h3>
            <p class="project-copy">A zero-config Neovim IDE for Odoo 8.0 through 19.0. LSP stubs, Doodba support, and XML→Python navigation without a config weekend.</p>
            <dl class="project-stats">
              <div><dt>Odoo</dt><dd>8–19</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Commits</dt><dd>30</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="project-link" href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/odoo.nvim">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>

          <article class="project project-ai">
            <p class="project-kind">AI <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Go + Terminal</p>
            <h3>OSEM</h3>
            <p class="project-copy">A session manager for OpenCode. SQLite queries 520× faster than parsing the CLI, with fuzzy search, bookmarks, and tmux windows.</p>
            <dl class="project-stats">
              <div><dt>Faster</dt><dd>520×</dd></div>
              <div><dt>License</dt><dd>MIT</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="project-link" href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/osem">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>

          <article class="project project-oca">
            <p class="project-kind">Connectivity <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Go + Cuba</p>
            <h3>Conecta</h3>
            <p class="project-copy">One CLI for ETECSA portal login, WiFi hotspot sharing, WireGuard VPN, and speed tests, built for the realities of connectivity in Cuba.</p>
            <dl class="project-stats">
              <div><dt>Interfaces</dt><dd>TUI + CLI</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Commits</dt><dd>37</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="project-link" href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/conecta">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>

          <article class="project project-owl">
            <p class="project-kind">OWL <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> QML + Omarchy</p>
            <h3>Omarchy Agents</h3>
            <p class="project-copy">A bar panel that watches every AI subscription on the machine and turns usage records into limits, balances, and reset times.</p>
            <dl class="project-stats">
              <div><dt>Surface</dt><dd>QML panel</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Input</dt><dd>File watcher</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="project-link" href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/omarchy-agents">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>

          <article class="project project-owl">
            <p class="project-kind">OWL <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Python</p>
            <h3>Hacking OWL</h3>
            <p class="project-copy">Experiments with OWL, the Odoo web framework: a custom web client and reusable components for people who want to see how the pieces fit.</p>
            <dl class="project-stats">
              <div><dt>Stars</dt><dd>9</dd></div>
              <div><dt>License</dt><dd>Apache-2.0</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="project-link" href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/hacking-owl">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>
        </div>

        <details class="more-projects">
          <summary>More experiments <span>5 repos</span></summary>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/odoodevforge">OdooDevForge</a> — a proof of concept that generates an Odoo module from natural language.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/owl-app">OWL app</a> — a small to-do application built with OWL.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/simple">SIMple</a> — an Android app for ETECSA services, GPLv3 and Material You.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/saldoacuba">SaldoACuba</a> — a PHP service for Cuban mobile balances from 2018.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/antoniodavid/omarchy-workspaces">Omarchy Workspaces</a> — a QML workspace switcher for the Omarchy desktop.</li>
          </ul>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section oca-section" id="oca" aria-labelledby="oca-title">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="section-label">04 / OCA wins</p>
          <h2 id="oca-title">Ten merged changes. Eight repositories.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">The Odoo Community Association runs on review. These are the changes that survived it, plus the one still open on purpose.</p>
        </header>

        <dl class="oca-summary">
          <div><dt>Submitted</dt><dd>37</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Repositories</dt><dd>19</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Merged</dt><dd>10</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Reviews</dt><dd>53</dd></div>
        </dl>

        <ul class="oca-grid" aria-label="Selected OCA pull requests">
          <li class="oca-card">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/delivery-carrier/pull/1079">
                <span class="oca-year">2026</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">delivery-carrier</span>
                <span class="oca-title">EasyPost carrier integration for Odoo 17</span>
                <span class="badge badge-merged">Merged</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          <li class="oca-card">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/delivery-carrier/pull/1082">
                <span class="oca-year">2026</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">delivery-carrier</span>
                <span class="oca-title">EasyPost migration to Odoo 18</span>
                <span class="badge badge-merged">Merged</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          <li class="oca-card">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/bank-statement-import/pull/864">
                <span class="oca-year">2025</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">bank-statement-import</span>
                <span class="oca-title">Plaid statement import migration to 18.0</span>
                <span class="badge badge-merged">Merged</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          <li class="oca-card">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/reporting-engine/pull/969">
                <span class="oca-year">2025</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">reporting-engine</span>
                <span class="oca-title">Spreadsheet dashboard migration for bi_view_editor</span>
                <span class="badge badge-merged">Merged</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          <li class="oca-card">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/reporting-engine/pull/968">
                <span class="oca-year">2025</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">reporting-engine</span>
                <span class="oca-title">bi_view_editor migration to 17.0</span>
                <span class="badge badge-merged">Merged</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          <li class="oca-card">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/stock-logistics-reporting/pull/404">
                <span class="oca-year">2025</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">stock-logistics-reporting</span>
                <span class="oca-title">Valued picking report configuration</span>
                <span class="badge badge-merged">Merged</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          <li class="oca-card">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/pos/pull/1309">
                <span class="oca-year">2025</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">pos</span>
                <span class="oca-title">pos_margin migration to 17.0</span>
                <span class="badge badge-merged">Merged</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          <li class="oca-card">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/website/pull/1095">
                <span class="oca-year">2025</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">website</span>
                <span class="oca-title">website_local_font migration to 17.0</span>
                <span class="badge badge-merged">Merged</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          <li class="oca-card">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/l10n-spain/pull/4083">
                <span class="oca-year">2025</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">l10n-spain</span>
                <span class="oca-title">IGIC accounts 112 and 113</span>
                <span class="badge badge-merged">Merged</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          <li class="oca-card">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/partner-contact/pull/1728">
                <span class="oca-year">2024</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">partner-contact</span>
                <span class="oca-title">partner_country_lang migration to 14.0</span>
                <span class="badge badge-merged">Merged</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          <li class="oca-card oca-card-open">
              <a class="oca-card-link" href="https://github.com/OCA/l10n-usa/pull/166">
                <span class="oca-year">Open</span>
                <span class="oca-repo">l10n-usa</span>
                <span class="oca-title">Bill.com two-way integration</span>
                <span class="badge badge-open">Open for review</span>
              </a>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <div class="oca-note">
          <p><strong>Teamwork, in public.</strong> 78 pull requests reviewed across 34 repositories and 28 authors. 53 of those reviews are in OCA, across 26 repositories and 22 authors.</p>
          <p class="source-line">Verified from public GitHub search on 30 October 2026.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section method-section" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="section-label">05 / Method</p>
          <h2 id="method-title">The part that does not fit in a screenshot.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">The interesting question is not whether the code compiles. It is whether the next person can trust it, change it, and ship it on a Friday.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="method-grid">
          <article class="method-card">
            <span class="method-number">01</span>
            <p class="method-tag">Spec</p>
            <h3>Spec before code.</h3>
            <p>ODF starts with a route, a context manifest, and a gate. The goal is the right change, not the first change.</p>
            <p class="method-evidence">11 agents · 51 skills · policy gates</p>
          </article>
          <article class="method-card">
            <span class="method-number">02</span>
            <p class="method-tag">Test</p>
            <h3>Test the contract.</h3>
            <p>1,477 unit tests, 331 YAML tests, and 18 harness tests in ODF. This page ships with its own regression suite.</p>
            <p class="method-evidence">TDD · 10 tagged releases</p>
          </article>
          <article class="method-card">
            <span class="method-number">03</span>
            <p class="method-tag">Review</p>
            <h3>Review as a teammate.</h3>
            <p>78 pull requests reviewed across 34 repositories and 28 authors. 53 of those reviews are in OCA, across 26 repositories.</p>
            <p class="method-evidence">53 OCA reviews</p>
          </article>
          <article class="method-card">
            <span class="method-number">04</span>
            <p class="method-tag">Ship</p>
            <h3>Ship with evidence.</h3>
            <p>Small, reviewable changes, Conventional Commits, tagged releases, and docs that tell the next person where the seams are.</p>
            <p class="method-evidence">MIT · changelog · docs</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section timeline-section" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="section-label">06 / Trajectory</p>
          <h2 id="timeline-title">From a first Odoo module to a public toolchain.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">Learn the framework, learn the community, then build the tools that make both easier for the next person.</p>
        </header>

        <ol class="timeline">
          <li>
            <time datetime="2018">2018</time>
            <h3>First public build</h3>
            <p>SaldoACuba, a PHP service for Cuban mobile balances. The start of shipping in public.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <time datetime="2019">2019</time>
            <h3>Odoo 12 in production</h3>
            <p>GeniusCentral addon: connecting Odoo to a retail catalog.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <time datetime="2022">2022</time>
            <h3>Python backend</h3>
            <p>FastAPI, services, scripts, and glue. Python becomes the default tool.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <time datetime="2023">2023</time>
            <h3>OWL experiments</h3>
            <p>A custom OWL web client and app prototypes. Nine stars on hacking-owl.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <time datetime="2024">2024</time>
            <h3>First OCA merge</h3>
            <p>partner_country_lang to 14.0 in partner-contact survives review.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <time datetime="2025">2025</time>
            <h3>OCA breadth</h3>
            <p>Delivery, banking, POS, reporting, website, and localization. 53 reviews so far.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <time datetime="2026">2026</time>
            <h3>Toolchain year</h3>
            <p>ODF, odoo.nvim, OSEM, and Conecta. 290 merged pull requests in total.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="toolbox-section" aria-labelledby="toolbox-title">
      <div class="container toolbox-inner">
        <h2 id="toolbox-title">Toolbox</h2>
        <ul class="chips">
          <li>Python</li>
          <li>Odoo 8–19</li>
          <li>TypeScript</li>
          <li>Go</li>
          <li>Lua</li>
          <li>QML</li>
          <li>PostgreSQL</li>
          <li>SQLite</li>
          <li>Docker</li>
          <li>Neovim</li>
